{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed","id":1107025,"title":"What if the Technocracy had Never Existed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-23T08:49:48-07:00","id":1107025,"title":"What if the Technocracy had Never Existed?","content":"I don't really know a lot about Mage's metaplot, but for the purposes of one my summer chronicles, I'm rewriting how cWoD history unfolded. One of my necessary assumptions is that the Technocracy nor it's precursors (the Order of Reason, right?) were ever founded. Thus, I have the following questions:<br /> <br /> Is it necessary, for human technological development, to have the Order of Reason or the Technocracy? Why not say humans just discovered the scientific method as an reaction to the Dark Ages and its creatures (vampires, werewolves, mages etc.)?<br /> <br /> The council of traditions would never be created, right?<br /> <br /> What other events and developments could be entailed by that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:08:14-07:00","id":1107028,"title":"","content":"A lot of this depends on just how influential you think the Technocracy and Traditions are. History, the way Mage tells it, is very closely tied to the spread of the Technocracy. It is not specifically necessary for the Technocracy to exist for the scientific method to arise, but would it be as effective without their backing? Depending on how flexible reality is (and I go with the interpretation that it's really flexible) they are responsible for much of modern technology. Even if they aren't it's hard to say they weren't integral to its spread. I'd say that without some major faction trying to unify everyone in a single paradigm the world would be more balkanized, magically. <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that other stabilizing or conquering groups couldn't have arisen. The Order of Hermes was in a position to spread their ideas to the world if the Order of Reason didn't, for instance. Not many of them would push a technological paradigm, though.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:13:23-07:00","id":1107030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed#post1107025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really know a lot about Mage's metaplot, but for the purposes of one my summer chronicles, I'm rewriting how cWoD history unfolded. One of my necessary assumptions is that the Technocracy nor it's precursors (the Order of Reason, right?) were ever founded. Thus, I have the following questions:<br /> <br /> Is it necessary, for human technological development, to have the Order of Reason or the Technocracy? Why not say humans just discovered the scientific method as an reaction to the Dark Ages and its creatures (vampires, werewolves, mages etc.)?<br /> <br /> The council of traditions would never be created, right?<br /> <br /> What other events and developments could be entailed by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The scientific method was a construct of the Order of Reason designed to make reality a lot more stable and to bring the power of the awakened into the hands of the unawakened. Because reality in Ascension is fluid, nothing is discovered so much as created and enforced. Without the order of reason it's possible that a construct of belief similar in essence to the scientific method would come about, but without the strength of numbers and organisation that the assembled Order of Reason would have provided, there is no real way it would become the prevailing paradigm, at best it would approach another craft, perhaps a disparate form within a larger whole like the Order of Hermes of the Solificati, at worse it would be a niche idea completely void of all the trappings we associate with technology today.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason was assembled primarily as a way to combat the threat of the Order of Hermes and their increasing reaches of power and tyranny. Without the Order of Reason, the Hermetics would be able to continue rising unopposed. In this alternative history it's possible that other forces would try to assemble to combat this group, otherwise the future would be very Hermetic, with awakened magic being an elite art that only the most learned and fearsom of mages would even be allowed to consider. Power would define control.<br /> <br /> In effect, the Hermetics would become all the worst aspects of the Technocracy, and what's worse is that as their arts have been around much longer than Science, they may not ever need to deal with paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T09:37:48-07:00","id":1107037,"title":"","content":"Either Hermetic or Messianic.<br /> <br /> Hermetics were weakened after the 1rst Massa War, If the Messianics (that, btw, included the Gabrielites, that would be part of the strong arm of the OoR) had put their game together and took control of the growing influence of the church, they could have upset the balance of power and nowdays mages could be hidding from the Theocracy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, powder wouldn't have been invented and weaponized in Europe so early (it's explicitly stated that Craftmasons pushed this) and trade would suffer a set back without the High Guild and the explorers of the OoR. You could argue that the Age of Exploration would have come very late or never, allowing native americans grow their empires unopposed. Who knows, maybe America would be ruled by an Incaic/Aztec empire of magic users, or something like that.<br /> <br /> Without the armamentistic power of Europe rising, the whole world would be very different. Imagine that. <hr /><br /> Of course, this it's less so if you believe that the world doesn't depend so much on the Consensus. or that humanity has enough autodetermination to choose the path of technology without the OoR guiding hand. In the second case humanity could be helped by making OoH enemies powerful enough to impede their dominance, but not enought to win","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-23-2017, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:44:13-07:00","id":1107111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed#post1107025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it necessary, for human technological development, to have the Order of Reason or the Technocracy? Why not say humans just discovered the scientific method as an reaction to the Dark Ages and its creatures (vampires, werewolves, mages etc.)?<br /> <br /> The council of traditions would never be created, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The over all rule of thumb for the entire WoD back in the day was that supernaturals don't control or direct human culture and development so much as they latch on to it and exploit it for their own purposes. One of Mage's main themes was always the problem of hubris among the Awakened, and part of that was the Technocracy's belief that they were responsible for all of human technological development. <br /> <br /> The Scientific Method goes back as far as Aristotle, if not further. <br /> <br /> And, yes, without the threat of the Order of Reason, then the Council of Traditions, and even some of the Traditions themselves, would never have formed. <br /> <br /> If I had to guess, the mundane world would largely continue to look a lot like it does in real life, just a little darker and grittier owing to the various supernatural influences in general (dark spirits, the sense that there are bad things and conspiracies in the shadows, an increased level of xenophobia and somewhat justified paranoia on the part of everyone, a somewhat starker divide between the realms of control and anarchy, as well as between mainstream culture and counter culture). <br /> <br /> From a mystical standpoint, instead of Traditions and an Ascension War, you've probably got a bunch of small fellowships/cabals/conspiracies all competing with each other to protect their own turf and advance their own agendas, sometimes working together against mutual threats like the Nephandi or the like. Groups like the Order of Hermes (or perhaps just a few of their Houses if the group collapsed in some sort of civil war infighting at some point in the past), the Old Faith, the Wu Lung, the Knights Templar, the Children of Knowledge, the Joybringers, the Bata'a, an independent Syndicate that looks more like the Hermetic House Fortunae, and so on. This is probably the sort of setting where the Hollow Ones would shine and be a good default starting place for PCs. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T14:58:19-07:00","id":1107127,"title":"","content":"Err no. The Scientific Method as a named concept goes back as far as Francis Bacon. Because Francis Bacon invented it in the 1600's. Prior to that you had similar studies, but such things are not science. As Science had yet to exist.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the whole premise of Mage is that literally every human on the planet is a mage. Even the sleepers have their power. Not to mention that Werewolf has litteral great spirits of hate the killing of which would largely remove racism from human society. Mage blatantly holds that Mages are responsible for most developments in human history. It wasn't until the Order of Reason gave the sleepers a framework to work with that non mages inventing things became a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T15:19:03-07:00","id":1107134,"title":"","content":"Well, thanks for all the answers, guys. Now I need a good excuse for all the scientific development since the early modern age. Maybe I should just ignore the whole metaphysics and say the humans can develop whatever their reasonings allow them.<br /> <br /> Or, if the paradigm is still a think I could assume the whole of humanity was responsible for the weakening of the magic. The same reason (atheism, relativism etc.) could prevent religion-based magicians from becoming the new rulers (no theocracy). <br /> <br /> If the world looks the basically same (maybe darker, ok) I could suppose there are other factions barring the supernatural control of society, such as the Witch Hunters. Mage-wise, the Order of Hermers could be weakened by the Tremere, and the Massasa War is still an important conflict in the modern nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T15:31:15-07:00","id":1107140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, the whole premise of Mage is that literally every human on the planet is a mage. Even the sleepers have their power. Not to mention that Werewolf has litteral great spirits of hate the killing of which would largely remove racism from human society. Mage blatantly holds that Mages are responsible for most developments in human history. It wasn't until the Order of Reason gave the sleepers a framework to work with that non mages inventing things became a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you believe every inventor of ancient civilizations, including roman architects whose works were admired by the man of the Renaissance, was Awakened<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I should just ignore the whole metaphysics and say the humans can develop whatever their reasonings allow them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recomend to do this. You don't need to ignore any of the methapysics, just part of the metaplot that it's more ego boost for mages and their place in the world than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T15:56:13-07:00","id":1107144,"title":"","content":"Or alternatively I believe that they were assistants to the guy who was awakened. What is a road network but a vast correspondence effect allowing one to quickly travel along it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T16:02:44-07:00","id":1107145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107140#post1107140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I recomend to do this. You don't need to ignore any of the methapysics, just part of the metaplot that it's more ego boost for mages and their place in the world than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:08:40-07:00","id":1107153,"title":"","content":"Also, you kind of do have to strongly stomp on the concept of a Subjective universe if you go with this. Because Science runs on predictable laws that stay the same. IF those exist then science can be done to discover them. If laws like that don't exist, as mage posits, then science is useless. Hence why Science is just a faction of mages in mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T18:16:28-07:00","id":1107167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107134#post1107134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, thanks for all the answers, guys. Now I need a good excuse for all the scientific development since the early modern age. Maybe I should just ignore the whole metaphysics and say the humans can develop whatever their reasonings allow them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should do that whether you dump the metaphysics or not. The two aren't contradictory. Humans are smart, they are going to make advances in whatever environment they happen to be in. That doesn't hinder the Technocracy, it actively helps them. It means they don't have to introduce most of the inventions, they can just spread their paradigm and let people do most of the heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> That's one of the biggest advantages the Technocracy has, it's methods are very user friendly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107153#post1107153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you kind of do have to strongly stomp on the concept of a Subjective universe if you go with this. Because Science runs on predictable laws that stay the same. IF those exist then science can be done to discover them. If laws like that don't exist, as mage posits, then science is useless. Hence why Science is just a faction of mages in mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually disagree on this one. You don't need things to be predictable throughout all of history, you just need them to be predictable for long enough that people can start working with them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-23-2017, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T19:09:57-07:00","id":1107177,"title":"","content":"Exactly, I agree 100% with Ramnesis<br /> <br /> All humans are mages and thus can shape reality with effort and will. It's just that some are slower than others, and some are more conscious than others of this process (and, thus, can manipulate the process).<br /> <br /> Wise mages have discovered arround the modern era that reality it's consensual, and thus that they can shape it at a very largue scale by social manipulation. BUT, in the end, social manipulation it's just pushing people where you want it to go. Now you need to ask yourself if the process that made a lot (but not all) people incline to reason, and, latter, science, can happen naturally...I don't think it's such a blasphemy to say that this is possible.<br /> <br /> As proof that humans can shape Reality without the active help of mages I offer this:<br /> <br /> In DA: Mage Magic was &quot;dying&quot;. Old spells started to fail and No Technocracy, no Mage group, did this consciously, some mages believed it was the end of times...but it wasn't, magick was just changing. Reality was changing in responce to the turmoils of Europe and a good part of the world. A proto-Consensus was slowly being born thanks to the Curch's attempts to unify Europe under their paradigm, and if Mages had anything to do with that, it was without their knowledge.<br /> <br /> If the sheppards aren't watching the sheeps, who knows where they will go? The masses are powerful whether this power it's used consciously by a secret organization or subconsciously by the people <hr />This is how you justify Scientific Consensus without the Illuminati at the wheel, in my opinion:<br /> <br /> If science developed without the guiding hand of the OoR, then it's likely to be the product of one or more unenlightened societies that originally formed arround the ideas of ancient philosophers and improved uppon them with pure human ingenuity. These seemingly ludic societies prospered and grow in influence and numbers, perhaps thanks to the effort of a charismatic leader unltil they reached a critical mass and their theories started to sound less and less far fetched. They didn't know (just as the Church in DA didn't know) that they were changing the way the universe works with their new ideas and proto-marketing, and they were left alone to prosper by mages for some reason (likely a vicious mage war between various factions, coupled with a disdain for &quot;mere mortals&quot;. Tremere alone won't do the trick because they would only impair the OoH). <hr /><br /> Of course, I'm not impliyng that this will be the likely outcome of a Mage without the OoR. We don't and can't know how would such a world be because the Technocracy it's such an intergral part of Mage's history that removing it leaves a blank area arround everyhing since the 1200. As far as I know, the Aztecs could be ruling earth with blood magic and Mayan technomagic if the Technocracy hadn't existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-23-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T19:40:38-07:00","id":1107183,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1119_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1119\" data-vbnamecard=\"1119\">Primal Flame</a> :<br /> <br /> Now, there's one question than I have to make:<br /> <br /> When you say that you don't want a world with Technocracy...you mean a world without Technocracy: the secret society that controls science?...or a world without Technomancers? Because these are two very different beasts.<br /> <br /> If it's the first, then what impedes/impeded another group of Technomancers to take the mantle of science?. One has to think the reasons behind this lack of science-pushers among mages even without Big Brother.<br /> <br /> If it's the second, then you will have to change the rules of the setting to disallow scientific paradigms as valid magical paradigms...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T20:31:15-07:00","id":1107197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107183#post1107183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1119_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1119\" data-vbnamecard=\"1119\">Primal Flame</a> :<br /> <br /> Now, there's one question than I have to make:<br /> <br /> When you say that you don't want a world with Technocracy...you mean a world without Technocracy: the secret society that controls science?...or a world without Technomancers? Because these are two very different beasts.<br /> <br /> If it's the first, then what impedes/impeded another group of Technomancers to take the mantle of science?. One has to think the reasons behind this lack of science-pushers among mages even without Big Brother.<br /> <br /> If it's the second, then you will have to change the rules of the setting to disallow scientific paradigms as valid magical paradigms...</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question.<br /> <br /> I want my WoD to be as Gothic as possible, and when I talk Gothic I mean informed by the notions of barbarism, fanaticism and obscurantism the generations of the 1790s-1830s associated with the Long Night. So, technology and science would be the domain of humans, and sorcery the domain of those confined to the night, or to the shadows. It means no Technocracy and no technomancers, I guess.<br /> <br /> Also, I want my WoD to be informed by the Christian myth of VtM and DtF (that's why I don't know what to do with werewolves, btw). Hermeticism, theurgy and other forms of magic described in Dark Ages: Mage seem to conform better to this pre-modern outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1119,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","user":"Primal Flame","date":". 06-23-2017, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T23:59:52-07:00","id":1107236,"title":"","content":"No technomancers is a difficult thing. It depends on where to draw the line.<br /> Many Mages could be described as technomancers using non standard technology.<br /> Rotes are a form of technology.<br /> <br /> If you just want to purge modern technology from being used for magick, not a problem if it is not around.<br /> But if there is, why shouldn't some mages use it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:01:26-07:00","id":1107344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question.<br /> <br /> I want my WoD to be as Gothic as possible, and when I talk Gothic I mean informed by the notions of barbarism, fanaticism and obscurantism the generations of the 1790s-1830s associated with the Long Night. So, technology and science would be the domain of humans, and sorcery the domain of those confined to the night, or to the shadows. It means no Technocracy and no technomancers, I guess.<br /> <br /> Also, I want my WoD to be informed by the Christian myth of VtM and DtF (that's why I don't know what to do with werewolves, btw). Hermeticism, theurgy and other forms of magic described in Dark Ages: Mage seem to conform better to this pre-modern outlook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, from the metaphysical side...yes this changes a lot. You're probably better doing as Enginseer said and scraping the &quot;subjective reality&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> This usually works on the grounds that science it's undistinguishable from magic (as was stated before, &quot;humans are mages and shape reality with their belief&quot;), but there needs to be a very big difference between magick and science in order for mages to be unable to choose science as their Paradigm...you may not need to scrape ALL of Paradigm mechanics, but at the very least we're faced with a mage in wich belief ISN'T what allows mages to change reality. Thus Paradigms are much less of a big deal.<br /> <br /> Metaphysicaly, this it's kind of a big deal...much bigger than just rewritting a few hundred years of history .<br /> <br /> So, reality isn't subjective, and magick doesn't come from belief...<br /> <br /> I have these ideas:<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0 Science works because the world it's objective, or at least objective enough to be studied...this may not be absolutely necessary (even in Demon human belief shapes reality a little), but simplifies a lot because we're accustomed for science to work that way in our daily lives.<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0<br /> Mages opperate as Demon says they do: They are the humans that somehow keept the Babel flame alive. And thanks to their humanity (their godly spark), they have the power to violate and reinvent these hidden laws.<br /> <br /> They may be the inheritors of Nephilim that survived the purgue and managed to teach what they knew (these would be the Wyck of the Verbena), or maybe it was another force that keept alive this forbidden fruit.<br /> <br /> 3\u00b0<br /> Paradigms were inherited from immemorial time as ways to explain this enlightened knowledge and power in a way that human minds can understand. Much like reality broke appart at the Fall, and humans stopped being able to speak the Adanic language, Paradigms are the shattered knowledge of Babel.<br /> <br /> Why?, because:<br /> <br /> 4\u00b0 Mages don't just Awaken, choose a Paradigm, and shape Reality...they CAN'T control their powers until they're teached one of the Pardigms that descended from Babel. This way a mage can't just believe whatever he want's (wich may include science), Paradigms are restricted. You could say that when mages overcome their Instruments, it's because they start to recover the old truths of Babel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:54:21-07:00","id":1107367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107127#post1107127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err no. The Scientific Method as a named concept goes back as far as Francis Bacon. Because Francis Bacon invented it in the 1600's. Prior to that you had similar studies, but such things are not science. As Science had yet to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Aristotle advocated and used inductive and deductive reasoning to develop and test theories and observations. His students of the Peripatetic School passed this on in the form of the Organon, and it's section on Posterior Analytics was one of the cornerstones of Medieval and Renaissance syllogistic logic. Francis Bacon's Novum Organon was a great leap forward because he advocated replacing syllogism with direct observation and experimental research. But Robert Grasseteste and Roger Bacon had already done this several hundred years earlier. And this process was further refined by Sir Isaac Newton and Galileo, then by Hans Christian Orsted, and Karl Popper, and has continued to be improved upon with things like peer review and double blind studies since then. <br /> <br /> What we think of as &quot;the Scientific Method&quot; did not spring whole cloth from someone's head. It's a process that evolved over the centuries, with a number of smart and talented people building on the work of those who came before them. As Newton said, &quot;If I see further, it is by standing on the shoulders of giants.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T10:56:24-07:00","id":1107369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107344#post1107344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2\u00b0<br /> Mages opperate as Demon says they do: They are the humans that somehow keept the Babel flame alive. And thanks to their humanity (their godly spark), they have the power to violate and reinvent these hidden laws.<br /> <br /> They may be the inheritors of Nephilim that survived the purgue and managed to teach what they knew (these would be the Wyck of the Verbena), or maybe it was another force that keept alive this forbidden fruit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea a lot, and wish D:tF had lasted long enough to allow it to be explored more. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T11:00:46-07:00","id":1107371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107197#post1107197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I want my WoD to be informed by the Christian myth of VtM and DtF (that's why I don't know what to do with werewolves, btw).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Malakim (sp?) from Demon became the Garou, but may not remember who/what they were. Or werewolves are what happens to vampires who let their Beast take over. Or they are people cursed by the Devil (or God).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T13:44:57-07:00","id":1107410,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys for the suggestions, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:49:40-07:00","id":1107668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107344#post1107344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1\u00b0 Science works because the world it's objective, or at least objective enough to be studied...this may not be absolutely necessary (even in Demon human belief shapes reality a little), but simplifies a lot because we're accustomed for science to work that way in our daily lives.<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0<br /> Mages opperate as Demon says they do: They are the humans that somehow keept the Babel flame alive. And thanks to their humanity (their godly spark), they have the power to violate and reinvent these hidden laws.<br /> <br /> They may be the inheritors of Nephilim that survived the purgue and managed to teach what they knew (these would be the Wyck of the Verbena), or maybe it was another force that keept alive this forbidden fruit.<br /> <br /> 3\u00b0<br /> Paradigms were inherited from immemorial time as ways to explain this enlightened knowledge and power in a way that human minds can understand. Much like reality broke appart at the Fall, and humans stopped being able to speak the Adanic language, Paradigms are the shattered knowledge of Babel.<br /> <br /> Why?, because:<br /> <br /> 4\u00b0 Mages don't just Awaken, choose a Paradigm, and shape Reality...they CAN'T control their powers until they're teached one of the Pardigms that descended from Babel. This way a mage can't just believe whatever he want's (wich may include science), Paradigms are restricted. You could say that when mages overcome their Instruments, it's because they start to recover the old truths of Babel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a great &quot;default&quot; way to handle a Vampire/Demon/Wraith focused version of the WoD. It would probably work well if Werewolves are &quot;de-Umbra-fied&quot; and &quot;de-Wyrmed&quot; and made into ferocious man-beasts that are typically the result of some kind of curse (kinda like vampires, but different enough to make it a worthwhile distinction)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:03:51-07:00","id":1107724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107668#post1107668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like a great &quot;default&quot; way to handle a Vampire/Demon/Wraith focused version of the WoD. It would probably work well if Werewolves are &quot;de-Umbra-fied&quot; and &quot;de-Wyrmed&quot; and made into ferocious man-beasts that are typically the result of some kind of curse (kinda like vampires, but different enough to make it a worthwhile distinction)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have them believing something similar to the whole Gaia/Wyrm cosmology, just without any really objective proof that they're correct. Or perhaps tweak it a bit so that they're sort of a dark Christian version of KotE's Devil Tigers, monsters created by God to prey upon and terrify the wicked and sinful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T15:48:13-07:00","id":1107782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107668#post1107668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like a great &quot;default&quot; way to handle a Vampire/Demon/Wraith focused version of the WoD. It would probably work well if Werewolves are &quot;de-Umbra-fied&quot; and &quot;de-Wyrmed&quot; and made into ferocious man-beasts that are typically the result of some kind of curse (kinda like vampires, but different enough to make it a worthwhile distinction)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any relationship between the Wyrm and Oblivion?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T05:36:37-07:00","id":1107984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107724#post1107724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could have them believing something similar to the whole Gaia/Wyrm cosmology, just without any really objective proof that they're correct. Or perhaps tweak it a bit so that they're sort of a dark Christian version of KotE's Devil Tigers, monsters created by God to prey upon and terrify the wicked and sinful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to lump all Werewolves into a very tight focus that doesn't track with the quasi-multiculturism of most White Wolf games or with the idea of having different splats fulfill different functions, so YMMV on that. If you just want Werewolves to be some kind of generic &quot;scary forest monsters who were once people&quot; and don't really care about looking more deeply (kinda like the Sabbat was originally) that might work. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, those werewolves would be one &quot;Tribe&quot; and the others would come from other werewolf cultural archetypes - Norse derived wolfsarks, Greek werewolves of the line of Lycaon, those guys you are postulating as a very dark take on something similar to a reverse-Children of Gaia that arose from various werewolves grappling with understanding their condition in a Christian context, and so on. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd love to have the later version set up. Werewolves without the &quot;Garou Nation&quot;, without Gaia and the Triat, without ubiquitous spirit magic and a focus on the Umbra... Those might be a much better fit for a World of Darkness, particularly one on this Demon/Vampire/Wraith, Mages-not-Mages set-up.<br /> <br /> But it sounds like a TON of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T05:38:44-07:00","id":1107986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107782#post1107782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any relationship between the Wyrm and Oblivion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If you want there to be. There's definitely some stuff out there that suggests it. And if you're conflating things from the games to integrate them into something more cohesive, might make sense.<br /> <br /> Alternatively - NO, NEVER, HERESY<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T05:40:52-07:00","id":1107988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107782#post1107782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any relationship between the Wyrm and Oblivion?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Wraith, no. At least not in any direct sense. It depends on what relationship you needed them to have. What were you thinking of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T05:48:17-07:00","id":1107994,"title":"","content":"It depends if you buy the Technocrats' propaganda. They claim to be the ones who invented science but it seems like Sleepers are actually directing scientific advancement while the Technocracy just plays catch-up with the way their magic disguises itself.<br /> <br /> The latter makes them look very bad while the former seems too generous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T21:49:12-07:00","id":1108268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107988#post1107988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Wraith, no. At least not in any direct sense. It depends on what relationship you needed them to have. What were you thinking of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, really. Both just appear to work as the final destination of all other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:07:29-07:00","id":1108295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107782#post1107782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any relationship between the Wyrm and Oblivion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. When the Wyrm dies, it will fall into the embrace of Oblivion. <br /> <br /> All of Creation will succumb to the warm, loving arms of Oblivion. <br /> <br /> (She has missed you.)<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:38:33-07:00","id":1108348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1108268#post1108268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing, really. Both just appear to work as the final destination of all other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I dug up the relevant sidebar in Wraith 2nd:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Wraith 2nd, pg 284</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oblivion and the Wyrm<br /> <br /> Occult scholars in the know often confuse the Wyrm and Oblivion. Admittedly, each is a tremendous force, and in some ways a personification of destruction, but that is the only similarity. The Wyrm is active destruction and corruption, seeking to tear down all that exists. It is not content to wait for things to fall apart; it wishes to drag all down to ruin by the force of its actions.<br /> <br /> Oblivion, on the other hand, is patient, passive destruction. When things grow old and falter, as they all inevitably must, then and only then does Oblivion claim them. Even Spectres, in a very real sense, give themselves to Oblivion as opposed to being claimed by it.<br /> <br /> At the end of all things, when the Wyrm has destroyed all else, it will seek to destroy the only thing that remains: itself. By doing so it will gift itself to Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Some theorists postulate that they Wyrm and Oblivion are bound together in a tight balance, a sort of yin-yang of destruction, and that as the Wyrm grew in power Oblivion was forced to grow to match it and maintain their eternal equilibrium. However, there is little (if any) evidence to support this hypothesis, and hard proof is likely to be hard to come by.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you don't need to limit yourself to that. It's really about what makes your game work.<br /> <br /> Possible relationships could include:<br /> <br /> Oblivion is what is left when the Wyrm destroys something. That is, it is nothingness for the Wyrm to leave and the Wyld to fill.<br /> <br /> When the Wyrm was still a creature of balance it destroyed things purely, but it set that aside when it became a Corruptor. Oblivion is the pure annihilation it set aside.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is something the Wyrm feeds by destroying. Since the Wyrm no longer destroys, Oblivion is having to feed itself. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:40:08-07:00","id":1108400,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Thank your for all the interesting suggestions. I hope they include this sidebar in Wraith's 20th anniversary edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:33:51-07:00","id":1108565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1107994#post1107994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends if you buy the Technocrats' propaganda. They claim to be the ones who invented science but it seems like Sleepers are actually directing scientific advancement while the Technocracy just plays catch-up with the way their magic disguises itself.<br /> <br /> The latter makes them look very bad while the former seems too generous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think about it this way. The Technocracy is White Wolf. They put out a book filled with rules, designed with certain expectations in mind. And convince a bunch of players these rules are important.<br /> <br /> Now, once they put those rules out their, power gamers will come up with ways to game the system. It's the same with the Technocratic laws. They put them out their without thinking through every possible consequence of them and now we have sleepers coming up with novel applications of physics. This is the key difference, in my mind, between Enlightened Science and Awakened Magic.<br /> <br /> Awakened Magic can duplicate all the same toys, but it lacks that internal consistency that allows sleepers to tap into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T07:22:55-07:00","id":1108752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Awakened Magic can duplicate all the same toys, but it lacks that internal consistency that allows sleepers to tap into it. </div> </div> </div>Awakened Magic It's no different of Enlightened Science in any way. RAW. As per Guide to the Technocracy and M20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, once they put those rules out their, power gamers will come up with ways to game the system. It's the same with the Technocratic laws. They put them out their without thinking through every possible consequence of them and now we have sleepers coming up with novel applications of physics. This is the key difference, in my mind, between Enlightened Science and Awakened Magic. </div> </div> </div>What constitutes &quot;the key difference&quot; isn't the only thing that is only &quot;in your mind&quot;, the very idea that there is a difference it's headcanon, no different in any way from my interpretation of &quot;magick works as Demon says&quot;. Don't sell it as the way things are. Sell it as the way you think things should be/could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-28-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T07:51:30-07:00","id":1108759,"title":"","content":"As Aleph says, Awakaned Magic and Enlightened Science are the same thing, just with different paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1108565#post1108565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened Magic can duplicate all the same toys, but it lacks that internal consistency that allows sleepers to tap into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Englightened Science is closer to the Consensus, so eventually, their stuff might get accepted by it, and anyone can replicate it with mundane science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T08:46:47-07:00","id":1108768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1108565#post1108565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakened Magic can duplicate all the same toys, but it lacks that internal consistency that allows sleepers to tap into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the difference is accessibility, not internal consistency. Plenty of Awakened Magic paradigms are internally consistent but long training periods, special understandings, or elitism keep them removed from regular people. Likewise, modern scientific principles and theories (i.e. the stuff the Sleepers are tapping into) do contradict each other, and this isn't seen as a problem (indeed it is an expected and necessary part of refining our theories).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:08:56-07:00","id":1108776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1108752#post1108752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awakened Magic It's no different of Enlightened Science in any way. RAW. As per Guide to the Technocracy and M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What constitutes &amp;quot;the key difference&amp;quot; isn't the only thing that is only &amp;quot;in your mind&amp;quot;, the very idea that there is a difference it's headcanon, no different in any way from my interpretation of &amp;quot;magick works as Demon says&amp;quot;. Don't sell it as the way things are. Sell it as the way you think things should be/could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are quite clearly differences in application. Paradigm isn't just window dressing.<br /> <br /> As demonstrated by the very real mechanical differences between technomancers and non technomancers.<br /> <br /> The fact that inventions have been developed using Technocrats methods by sleepers is a sign of a very clear difference between them and the traditions. The unawakened don't just decide to develop a new spell and actually go and do it.<br /> <br /> While awakened magic and enlightened science are of the same substance, and drawn from the same source, their vessels are very different indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T09:36:18-07:00","id":1108797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the difference is accessibility, not internal consistency. Plenty of Awakened Magic paradigms are internally consistent but long training periods, special understandings, or elitism keep them removed from regular people. Likewise, modern scientific principles and theories (i.e. the stuff the Sleepers are tapping into) do contradict each other, and this isn't seen as a problem (indeed it is an expected and necessary part of refining our theories).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my interpretation too.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't think that Enginseer's headcanon it's horrendous, I do think it contradicts established canon rather heavily...the differency cannot be anything but nomenclature if you don't want to stray from the canon. Thus, the reason of why &quot;science worked for the mundanes in the end (after we suffered a lot of Paradox convincing them), and magic not&quot; has to be searched not in the <i>magick itself </i>but in the different approach they took with the rest of the world (Hermetism didn't work because Hermetics refused to teach it to the masses), or maybe in how masive it's their reach (Hermetisc don't work because Hermetics didn't conquered America throwing fireballs), or in another tangential aspect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T10:12:19-07:00","id":1108811,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As demonstrated by the very real mechanical differences between technomancers and non technomancers.<br /> <br /> The fact that inventions have been developed using Technocrats methods by sleepers is a sign of a very clear difference between them and the traditions. The unawakened don't just decide to develop a new spell and actually go and do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technomancers are part of the Traditions, since there's Technomancers in every Tradition from the Etherites with their &quot;nonsense&quot; theories to the Hermetics and their magical laptops and the technoshamans....and they all count as Technomancers as far as the sidebar in Revised it's concerned. A Scientific Mystic isn't less of a technomancer than your average Etherite...what it's this difference supposed to prove again?<br /> <br /> You think that aplying runes to computers to craft a magical talisman (a technomancer's practice as far as it can be done by an Etherite Scientific Mystic) can be learned and improved by the sleepers but buddhism mental techniques (requiring an internal focus, and thus a mystic paradigm) can't?.<br /> <br /> <i>Being a technomancer doesn't guarantee that your method can be studied and practiced by the sleepers </i>(or at least this wasn't enough for Etherites and their &quot;free energy&quot;), conversely, <i>being a mystic doesn't mean that your method can't contribute to sleeper life in a small way</i>, as many natural medicines were discovered by shamans and people that you would call &quot;mystics&quot;, martial arts supposedly come from the techniques that Akashicks developped, it's even stated in HTDT that chi/energy manipulation techniques like Reiki may work in the WoD because how mystics pushed them into the population...so there you have.<br /> <br /> Conversely, you can't proove that &quot;The unawakened don't just decide to develop a new spell and actually go and do it&quot; in a world where the Technocracy has the upper hand. <i>\u200bThings aren't that way, thus they CAN'T be that way!</i> it's a silly argument. There are many possible explanations of why things aren't that way (Ramnesis and lordmagnused offered two), even from the books, and untill I see, from the books, that mystics can't possibly teach sleepers to do their mojo even if they control the Consensus and they want to teach their methods, I'm not going to accept that it's impossible by the RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While awakened magic and enlightened science are of the same substance, and drawn from the same source, their vessels are very different indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the Etherite learning shamanism because shamanism IT'S SCIENCE!!!!, the one that can't abandon his drums because it's a technomancer. Then show me that a group of sleepers can develop this &quot;science&quot; easier than a group of martial artists can develop Akashick techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-28-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T15:07:07-07:00","id":1109421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1108811#post1108811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Technomancers are part of the Traditions, since there's Technomancers in every Tradition from the Etherites with their &quot;nonsense&quot; theories to the Hermetics and their magical laptops and the technoshamans....and they all count as Technomancers as far as the sidebar in Revised it's concerned. A Scientific Mystic isn't less of a technomancer than your average Etherite...what it's this difference supposed to prove again?<br /> <br /> You think that aplying runes to computers to craft a magical talisman (a technomancer's practice as far as it can be done by an Etherite Scientific Mystic) can be learned and improved by the sleepers but buddhism mental techniques (requiring an internal focus, and thus a mystic paradigm) can't?.<br /> <br /> <i>Being a technomancer doesn't guarantee that your method can be studied and practiced by the sleepers </i>(or at least this wasn't enough for Etherites and their &quot;free energy&quot;), conversely, <i>being a mystic doesn't mean that your method can't contribute to sleeper life in a small way</i>, as many natural medicines were discovered by shamans and people that you would call &quot;mystics&quot;, martial arts supposedly come from the techniques that Akashicks developped, it's even stated in HTDT that chi/energy manipulation techniques like Reiki may work in the WoD because how mystics pushed them into the population...so there you have.<br /> <br /> Conversely, you can't proove that &quot;The unawakened don't just decide to develop a new spell and actually go and do it&quot; in a world where the Technocracy has the upper hand. <i>\u200bThings aren't that way, thus they CAN'T be that way!</i> it's a silly argument. There are many possible explanations of why things aren't that way (Ramnesis and lordmagnused offered two), even from the books, and untill I see, from the books, that mystics can't possibly teach sleepers to do their mojo even if they control the Consensus and they want to teach their methods, I'm not going to accept that it's impossible by the RAW.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tell that to the Etherite learning shamanism because shamanism IT'S SCIENCE!!!!, the one that can't abandon his drums because it's a technomancer. Then show me that a group of sleepers can develop this &quot;science&quot; easier than a group of martial artists can develop Akashick techniques.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is relevant how? Technomancers are mechanically different from for lack of a better word 'traditional' mages. It doesn't matter if those Technomancers are Traditionalists or Technocrats, their abilities are <i>fundementally different</i> the different isn't enormous. But it's there.<br /> <br /> THEREFOR, Enlightened Science just being Awakened Magic with a different coat of paint on it is simplification to the point of deception. Yes, in a certain sense it's true. They use similar means. However the methodology and applications are insanely different. It's like trying to say that a hermetic invoking the name of a fire elemental to conjure flames is fundementally doing the exact same thing as an Akashic who focuses their chi to protect them from fire. Yes. In both cases it's just forces. But the two techniques are radically different and lend themselves to wildly different applications.<br /> <br /> And your right. Being a Technomancer doesn't guarantee that your method can be studied and practiced by the sleepers. The Etherites are proof enough of that. But Enlightened Science and Hypertech <i>were deliberately designed to be able to be studied and practiced by sleepers.</i><br /> <br /> Name a moment, in the dark ages lore, where sleepers without awakening developed a city shattering work of high ritual magic. Or blood Magic. Or whatever.<br /> <br /> Nuclear Bombs were developed by sleepers taking two things that the Union was working on and smashing them together with unexpected results.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T01:21:40-07:00","id":1109659,"title":"","content":"Pacts with infernal beings come to my mind.<br /> <br /> Barter your soul for destruction of a city is perfectly within Dark Age Lore IMO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T04:36:42-07:00","id":1109693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1109421#post1109421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Name a moment, in the dark ages lore, where sleepers without awakening developed a city shattering work of high ritual magic. Or blood Magic. Or whatever.<br /> <br /> Nuclear Bombs were developed by sleepers taking two things that the Union was working on and smashing them together with unexpected results.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there were one, would the Technocracy allow it to remain in the history books? Any great rituals that didn't fit the new truth would be erased entirely, banished to mythology, or called apocryphal. So with that in mind:<br /> <br /> The Salting of Carthage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:39:46-07:00","id":1109827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is relevant how? Technomancers are mechanically different from for lack of a better word 'traditional' mages. It doesn't matter if those Technomancers are Traditionalists or Technocrats, their abilities are <i>fundementally different</i> the different isn't enormous. But it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've missed my point. And you don't lack of a better word, the word it's &quot;mystic&quot; (it's right there in the section you've grabbed the rules of leaving instruments)<br /> <br /> M20 states that technomancers are so tied to their instruments because they believe that their power comes from their instruments. Metaphysics of magick sections also imply that they're just wrong, the source of their power it's fundamentally the same and they can't do the trick of casting without instruments because they're such brickheads. When they reach Arete 6, they can do the trick, unless they've been brainwashed by the Technocracy.<br /> You stated that the magick that one faction uses it's fundamentally different from the magick other factions use...quoting a mechanical difference doesn't prove that, because the mechanic could very well be &quot;just window dressing&quot;. If you use a hammer as dorstopper you're using a different mechanic for the object, but this doesn't make it less of a hammer.<br /> <br /> <b>However, this is entirely tangential, because the point you were trying to demonstrate wasn't that &quot;they employ magick in a different way&quot;, your point was that whatever method mystics use it's <i>incapable </i>of generating laws that then people can reproduce or study to &quot;improve misticism&quot;. </b>Wasn't this your whole point?<br /> <br /> <i>Well, then, answering your 1rst question: </i><br /> <br /> I was pointing out to the fact that, because not all technomagic can be reproduced, and mystically developed techniques seem to work for mundanes even in a world where suppoosedly &quot;technomancy it's the law&quot;, then it's debatable if you being a technomancer helps in any way to make your magic available to the public. Certainly it doesn't help the Traditionalist technomancers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Name a moment, in the dark ages lore, where sleepers without awakening developed a city shattering work of high ritual magic. Or blood Magic. Or whatever. </div> </div> </div>1\u00ba Why has to be city shattering? Most Traditions explicitly don't want sleepers to be able to shatter cities and would have tried to prevent such mystic arts to be developed. Unlike Iteration X, that thinks more firepower it's always better<br /> <br /> On the &quot;whatever&quot; departament:<br /> <br /> You could always train an army in the mistically developped, but now almost mundane, technique DO, then send them to trash down a city. Supposedly all martial arts come from Do, so you could argue that it was, at least, a &quot;body shattering&quot; contribution.<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba The Dark Ages weren't ruled by any Mystical Paradigm. MAGIC WAS DYING (for the hermetics, blood magicians, and few others). You're comparing apples and oranges, DA world isn't the same world of the Technocracy, high ritual never had the kind of support and acceptance technology has today (to the point that even religious fundamentalists use it), exept, perhaps, in ancient egypt.<br /> <br /> The only Paradigm that came close to Technocracy's in domain was that of the Church...and even that was in an isolated part of the world (Asia had other Paradigms)...In that sense, Nonsenses argument it's interesting, whitin Church's, Infernalism would allow to blast away cities...Infernalism: Path of Screams talks about how normal people in the renaissance was able to summon devils with horrid grimoires and whatnot...so, who knows?<br /> <br /> 3\u00ba Mystics were never very open with their arts. Again, you're comparing apples and oranges here, not beacause technomagic &quot;it's different&quot; but because the Order of Reason (a group of people, not a &quot;type&quot; of magick) wanted their stuff to be public, it's hard to prove that sleepers can't improve uppon mystic arts when they never had a chance to do so because mages hoarded their lore.<br /> <br /> This is, actully, a good argument for sleepers to develop science on their own even if the OoR never forms...they will want &quot;more&quot;, and mystics ain't giving you anything unless you pass trials, say oaths, and dedicate your life to them. And no one wants to do that. Rescuing the work of old philosophers make sense because they don't ask so much to get results.<br /> <br /> And about older ages: If ALL the bajillon of wonders of architecture built by the romans, egiptians, and whatnot are, to you, the work of magicians (as per older posts, I don't know if this has changed), then how can I prove that a certain mystical happening of the past happened for real and wasn't performed by mages...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there were one, would the Technocracy allow it to remain in the history books? Any great rituals that didn't fit the new truth would be erased entirely, banished to mythology, or called apocryphal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-30-2017, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:35:05-07:00","id":1109908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1109693#post1109693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there were one, would the Technocracy allow it to remain in the history books? Any great rituals that didn't fit the new truth would be erased entirely, banished to mythology, or called apocryphal. So with that in mind:<br /> <br /> The Salting of Carthage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were several incidents during the Punic Wars that would meet the criterion. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:54:39-07:00","id":1110900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107025-what-if-the-technocracy-had-never-existed?p=1108811#post1108811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, you can't proove that &quot;The unawakened don't just decide to develop a new spell and actually go and do it&quot; in a world where the Technocracy has the upper hand. <i>\u200bThings aren't that way, thus they CAN'T be that way!</i> it's a silly argument. There are many possible explanations of why things aren't that way (Ramnesis and lordmagnused offered two), even from the books, and untill I see, from the books, that mystics can't possibly teach sleepers to do their mojo even if they control the Consensus and they want to teach their methods, I'm not going to accept that it's impossible by the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Moreover, we know of at least one type of unAwakened being that can and do invent new spells: Vampires. Blood sorcerers research and develop new Rituals and Paths all the time. The first things that the Tremere accomplished after becoming vampires was invent blood magic Rituals, and they've been iterating on their methods ever since.<br /> <br /> And remember, vampires are some of the most Static creatures in the world. If they can create new magic, mortals should be able to as well. And both Sorcerer books, as I recall, confirm as much. It is, in fact, a thing that happens in WoD. The unAwakened are totally able to create new magic. It's just more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:21:43-07:00","id":1112373,"title":"","content":"I think a question that would have to be asked first is, is the WOD metaphysically idealistic or not? The books themselves are vague and contradictory on this issue. If WOD is metaphysically idealistic, then no technocracy would create a wildly different world, perhaps even one in which the earth is a flat surface riding on a turtle or something equally fantastical.<br /> <br /> If the WOD isn't metaphysically idealistic, then the rise of a world that looks mostly technocratic is inevitable. In a non-metaphysically-idealistic world, then the Technocracy is actually mostly just outright correct. Traditions aren't fighting to truly redefine the world in such a setting, they are just trying to keep a few things at the edges of reality alive. Conversely, the Technocrats aren't truly trying to define the world, they already have simply seen the actual reality. Instead, the Technocrats are just trying to destroy a few oddities at the fringes of reality.<br /> <br /> It's an important question, because it defines who is the hero of the story, yet it has wild mechanical effects under certain scenarios. If the Technocrats are just flat out right, then the Trads are promoting a genuinely dangerous reality cancer. It also means that a mostly technocratic world is inevitable even with no technocracy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the Traditions are right, then the world could be radically transformed by what amounts to successful paradigm politicking. It also means that there really shouldn't be things that are wildly vulgar under all circimstances. Which has some pretty wild, if situational, mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> White Wolf's crunch generally seems to take the first view, simply for the sake of balance. You need some things to just be wildly vulgar always if you don't want the power levels to be nuts. Yet much(but not all) of their fluff seems to take the second view, as fluff is not inherently concerned about power balance.<br /> <br /> This results in a sort of plot-hole where the crunch and the fluff tend to contradict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:19:31-07:00","id":1112661,"title":"","content":"There are various &quot;middle grounds&quot; between those polar opposites.<br /> <br /> Reality doesn't need to be ALL fixed nor ALL consensual.<br /> <br /> In fact, it's very convinient to have at least a few things fixed to build a Consensual methaphisic, albeit you can do some mental gymnastics to avoid the logical problems that arise (I.E: how humans were created?).<br /> <br /> You can have, for instance, a reality that on the surface it's objectively like our world, but the forces behind it are subjective. Magnets atract each other, in a Technocratic Paradigm this it's because electrons, but if Extatics ruled it's because love. In this world magnets are a thing, but electromagnets may not work (albeit in that world could be other ways to create artificial magnets)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-07-2017, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}